Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:50:06 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] episode_features: n_turns by the GT direction-vector rule,
 consecutive triggers merged

n_turns now follows prior.cognitive_map_generation.trajectory_direction_vectors
on the dense GT path: a segment whose direction has cosine < 0.8
(TRAJECTORY_KEYPOINT_SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD, > 36.87 deg) to the last kept
direction is a direction change; no cap of five; changes on consecutive
segments are merged into one turn.  n_turn_triggers keeps the unmerged
count.  Replaces the 1 m resampling with a 45 deg threshold, which split
corners between samples and missed them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013viJtZsLciemzz8VtLkwa1
